stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> REPORTED : Employee reports incident (initial state)

    REPORTED --> ASSIGNED : Technician assigned (manual / strategy)
    REPORTED --> CANCELLED : Reporter or Admin cancels ticket

    ASSIGNED --> IN_PROGRESS : Technician starts diagnosis / work
    ASSIGNED --> ASSIGNED : Technician or Admin reassigns
    ASSIGNED --> CANCELLED : Admin cancels ticket

    state IN_PROGRESS {
        [*] --> Diagnosing
        Diagnosing --> Remediating
        Remediating --> Testing
    }

    IN_PROGRESS --> PENDING_INFO : Technician requests clarification (pauses SLA)
    PENDING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : Reporter provides requested info (resumes SLA)

    IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : Technician provides resolution summary
    IN_PROGRESS --> ASSIGNED : Reassigned to different tier / specialist

    RESOLVED --> CLOSED : Reporter verifies and accepts resolution
    RESOLVED --> IN_PROGRESS : Reporter rejects resolution (reopened within 48h)
    RESOLVED --> CLOSED : System auto-closes after 48h inactivity

    CLOSED --> [*] : Terminal state (immutable)
    CANCELLED --> [*] : Terminal state (immutable)

    note right of PENDING_INFO
        SLA resolution clock is PAUSED while waiting for user info.
        Resumes immediately upon user submission.
    end note

    note left of CLOSED
        FORBIDDEN TRANSITIONS:
        - CLOSED -> Any state (strictly immutable)
        - CANCELLED -> Any state (strictly immutable)
        - REPORTED -> RESOLVED / CLOSED (must pass through IN_PROGRESS)
        - ASSIGNED -> CLOSED (must be resolved first)
        - PENDING_INFO -> RESOLVED (must return to IN_PROGRESS first)
    end note
